{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785994631491372001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"dink-hut-umbra","assignee":"","attestations":{"plan-review":{"algorithm":"HMAC-SHA256","author":"Iso Tester","head_sha":"810bd573c77ed258c8f4d21d7361970c0bf4d57d","key_id":"412fa5372ad877e0","kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: e5ec-2e8d-500a-4d2d","material: a9dd934ee063fa18","model: claude-sonnet-4-6","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 10","regver: 83e5f63ad06d893a","verified-at-sha:810bd573c77ed258c8f4d21d7361970c0bf4d57d"],"signature":"cb96183d08ed25fe0f74123369728d714919ca9a0d2f5b29f7b8ad5f3cc6bbb9","signed_at":1782781153336812000}},"author":"Joe Oakhart","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":7},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Joe Oakhart","body":"Root-caused during c7c5 dogfooding: the over-exploration/non-convergence was ToolStrategy's forced tool_choice preventing natural termination (A/B: >250 tool calls WITH it / timeout vs ~17 WITHOUT, same model/prompt/ticket; a Claude Code sonnet subagent: ~12) — NOT AutoStrategy per se. The completion verifier now uses RunRequest.output_strategy='extract' (run with no forced response_format -> natural termination in text -> tool-less with_structured_output extraction). This ticket remains: should review/code/scan also move off ToolStrategy (to 'extract' or AutoStrategy/ProviderStrategy) framework-wide? Prior-art: forcing the loop is the documented anti-pattern; bigger/reasoning models over-explore MORE.","timestamp":1781832672423741001}],"created_at":1781819188074875001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[{"link_uuid":"53b0eeaf-f1bc-475e-a43c-532d86c7dbb6","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c7c5-12ea-ad68-4690"}],"description":"## Status (rescoped 2026-06-29)\nThe spike's functional goal is MOOT. The framework already moved off forced-tool `ToolStrategy` entirely: the pydantic_ai runtime cutover means review/code/scan + the completion verifier all run on natural-termination output via `output_mode()` (`PromptedOutput`/`NativeOutput`) — there is no `ToolStrategy`/`AutoStrategy`/`ProviderStrategy` anywhere in `src/rebar`. So the BI-1 optional-None-leakage class the spike worried about is already structurally avoided, and an AutoStrategy/ProviderStrategy evaluation is no longer worth running.\n\nWhat remains is pure DOC HYGIENE: the now-stale \"disable extended thinking because forced tool-choice conflicts\" rationale still lingers in the runner/structured-output source comments and reads as if forced-tool is still in use.\n\n## Scope\n- Update/remove the stale \"disable thinking (forced tool-choice conflict)\" rationale in `src/rebar/llm/runner.py` (~lines 72-77) and `src/rebar/llm/structured.py` (~lines 11-12, 52-54) so it reflects the current pydantic_ai `PromptedOutput`/`NativeOutput` reality (keep any genuinely-still-true note as historical context, clearly labelled).\n- Record the decision in-ticket: the AutoStrategy/ProviderStrategy spike is superseded by the pydantic_ai cutover; no migration needed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Stale forced-tool/\"disable thinking\" rationale in `runner.py` + `structured.py` is corrected or removed (no comment implies forced `ToolStrategy` is the current mechanism).\n- [ ] Decision recorded: spike moot — superseded by the pydantic_ai runtime cutover (cite that no ToolStrategy/AutoStrategy/ProviderStrategy exists in `src/rebar`).\n- [ ] `make lint` + test suite pass.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/runner.py","reason":"Correct stale forced-tool/disable-thinking comment rationale (RunRequest fields + PydanticAIRunner docstring)"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/structured.py","reason":"Correct stale forced-tool framing; preserve live Anthropic-400 constraint as current reality"}]